  "summary_en": "Opinion piece by Ronald Arkin on the ethics of robots deceiving humans. Drawing on his group's research on deceptive robots, he contrasts deontological and consequentialist views, notes military acceptance of deception, and observes there are no guidelines for researchers. He suggests guidelines may be needed from the community or external bodies.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Robotic deception is under-discussed compared with other AI and robotics ethical risks.",
   "No guidelines currently exist for researchers working on robot deception.",
   "Deception may be beneficial in contexts such as search and rescue or dementia care.",
   "Guidelines may need to come from within the robotics community or from external bodies.",
   "The IEEE Global Initiative on Ethics of Intelligent and Autonomous Systems is addressing these questions."
